      "nativeFindings": "The corrected blue2H pattern has four symmetric equally separated sticks and inner sticks visibly about three times the outer height, giving a clear first-order1:3:3:1 quartet. The orange3H singlet and green3H triplet remain distinctly separated; the green pair of shorter outer sticks and taller central stick represent the qualitative1:2:1 triplet motif without a calibrated intensity scale. The formula CH3-C(=O)-O-CH2-CH3 is validC4H8O2: allC valence4 andO valence2. BlueOCH2~4.1ppm quartet, orangeacylCH3~2.1ppm singlet andgreenterminalCH3~1.3ppm triplet match actual proton environments/H counts. The IR carbonyl motif near1740cm^-1 points toC=O; absorption is upright and no contradictory calibrated horizontal axis was reintroduced. Secondary ethyl ester skeletal formula, IR device and NMR magnet are intact and appropriate. No new molecules, wrong functional class, overvalence, numerical scale or outside-region chemistry error is visible.",
